@startuml Product Search Flow - Algolia with Firestore Fallback
!pragma teoz true

actor "User" as User
participant "Flutter UI\n(SearchBar)" as UI
participant "HomeViewModel" as VM
participant "AlgoliaProductRepository" as Repo
participant "AlgoliaService" as AlgoliaService
participant "Algolia API" as Algolia
participant "Firestore" as Firestore
participant "ProductRepository\n(Firestore)" as FallbackRepo

autonumber

== Phase 1: Search Input (Debounced) ==

User -> UI: Types "laptop"
activate UI

UI -> UI: Start 500ms debounce timer

User -> UI: Types "laptops"
UI -> UI: Cancel previous timer\nRestart 500ms timer

note over UI
  **Debouncing prevents**
  excessive API calls
  during typing
end note

UI -> VM: onSearchChanged("laptops")
activate VM

VM -> VM: Update state\n(isLoading: true)

VM -> Repo: fetchProducts(\n  query: "laptops",\n  categoryId: null\n)
activate Repo

== Phase 2: Algolia Search (Happy Path) ==

Repo -> AlgoliaService: search(\n  query: "laptops",\n  filters: {isActive: true}\n)
activate AlgoliaService

AlgoliaService -> Algolia: POST /1/indexes/products/query\n{\n  query: "laptops",\n  filters: "isActive:true",\n  hitsPerPage: 20,\n  typoTolerance: true\n}
activate Algolia

Algolia -> Algolia: Search index\n- Typo tolerance\n- Ranking algorithm\n- Faceted filters

Algolia --> AlgoliaService: {\n  hits: [...],\n  nbHits: 47,\n  processingTimeMS: 52\n}
deactivate Algolia

AlgoliaService -> AlgoliaService: Convert Algolia hits\nto Product models

AlgoliaService --> Repo: List<Product>\n(47 products, 52ms)
deactivate AlgoliaService

Repo --> VM: ProductResult(\n  products: [...],\n  source: "algolia"\n)
deactivate Repo

VM -> VM: Update state\n{\n  products: [...],\n  isLoading: false,\n  searchQuery: "laptops"\n}

VM --> UI: State changed
deactivate VM

UI -> UI: Rebuild widget tree

UI --> User: Display 47 products\n(sorted by relevance)
deactivate UI

== Phase 3: Algolia Failure (Fallback Path) ==

User -> UI: Types "gaming mouse"
activate UI
UI -> VM: onSearchChanged("gaming mouse")
activate VM
VM -> Repo: fetchProducts("gaming mouse")
activate Repo

Repo -> AlgoliaService: search("gaming mouse")
activate AlgoliaService

AlgoliaService -> Algolia: POST /1/indexes/products/query
activate Algolia

Algolia --> AlgoliaService: ❌ 503 Service Unavailable
deactivate Algolia

AlgoliaService --> Repo: ❌ AlgoliaException(\n  "Service unavailable"\n)
deactivate AlgoliaService

note over Repo
  **Fallback mechanism**
  Catches Algolia errors
  and uses Firestore query
end note

Repo -> FallbackRepo: fetchProducts(\n  query: "gaming mouse"\n)
activate FallbackRepo

FallbackRepo -> Firestore: Query:\nwhere('isActive', '==', true)\n.where('keywords',\n  'array-contains-any',\n  ['gaming', 'mouse']\n)\n.orderBy('dateCreated', 'desc')
activate Firestore

Firestore --> FallbackRepo: DocumentSnapshot[]\n(14 products, 187ms)
deactivate Firestore

FallbackRepo -> FallbackRepo: Convert snapshots\nto Product models

FallbackRepo --> Repo: List<Product>\n(14 products, slower)
deactivate FallbackRepo

Repo --> VM: ProductResult(\n  products: [...],\n  source: "firestore_fallback"\n)
deactivate Repo

VM -> VM: Update state\n(products from Firestore)

VM --> UI: State changed
deactivate VM

UI --> User: Display 14 products\n(Firestore fallback)
deactivate UI

note over User, Firestore
  **Performance Comparison**
  Algolia: 50ms avg, typo-tolerant, ranked
  Firestore: 200ms avg, exact match only
  
  Fallback ensures 100% availability
  even if Algolia is down
end note

== Phase 4: Category Filter ==

User -> UI: Select "Electronics" category
activate UI

UI -> VM: onCategoryChanged(categoryId: 1)
activate VM

VM -> Repo: fetchProducts(\n  query: "laptops",\n  categoryId: 1\n)
activate Repo

Repo -> AlgoliaService: search(\n  query: "laptops",\n  filters: "isActive:true AND categoryId:1"\n)
activate AlgoliaService

AlgoliaService -> Algolia: POST with filters
activate Algolia
Algolia --> AlgoliaService: {\n  hits: [...],\n  nbHits: 32\n}
deactivate Algolia

AlgoliaService --> Repo: List<Product>\n(32 electronics)
deactivate AlgoliaService

Repo --> VM: ProductResult
deactivate Repo

VM --> UI: Updated state
deactivate VM

UI --> User: Display 32 products\n(filtered by category)
deactivate UI

@enduml
